# Highlight, the color behind a styled run (reference/common/text-formatting.md): page of 240 × 160 with margins of
# 20, page area of 200 × 120 from (20, 20). Size 10 with Line height 15; with the test metrics each character measures
# 5 pt. The highlight changes no box and no line: the image shows it, from the ascent to the descent of the font.
#   one:   a run in the middle of a line. y = 20.
#   lines: "aaaa bbbb cccc dddd eeee" in a box of 60, with "bbbb cccc dddd" highlighted: three lines, the highlight at
#          the end of the first and on the whole second, without the space the line break swallows. y = 35.
#   marks: bold, underline and strikethrough inside the run, which is a single rectangle, and a run with its own color
#          of text. y = 80.
#   more:  a highlighted superscript, whose rectangle is that of the line, and a link inside a highlighted run. y = 95.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 240
		Height: 160
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
				Line height: 15
				Markup: markdown
		For style: mark
			Typography:
				Highlight: #FFE680
		For style: alert
			Typography:
				Highlight: #B3261E
				Color: #FFFFFF
				Bold: true
		For style: sup
			Typography:
				Text position: superscript
				Highlight: #CDE8FF
		For style: narrow
			Box:
				Width: 60
	Section:
		Text: Vence el [15 de mayo]{mark}.
			Id: one
		Text: aaaa [bbbb cccc dddd]{mark} eeee
			Id: lines
			Style: narrow
		Text: Son [**12** de ++mayo++ y ~~13~~]{mark} y [NO]{alert}.
			Id: marks
		Text: Son m[2]{sup} y [ver [la web](https://stxt.dev)]{mark}.
			Id: more
